To create a project we just simply add a `:` at the end:
    ☐ To create a task we just simply press `Alt+Enter`
    ☐ There is some `grayed` out statistic to the right of the project name, that shows `count` of tasks etc..
    ☐ It will also show some time statistics if we give a task an estimated time with `@1h`
    
Timekeeping:
    ☐ We can add estimates: Lets say this one will take exactly @2h
        ☐ Another way is by using natural language @est(1 day and 2 hours)
    ✔ To complete a task we can press `Alt+D` , press again to undo it @done(25-09-14 21:28)
    ☐ To start a a task we can press `Alt-S`, press again to stop it.
    ☐ And to cancel we simply press `Alt-C`, press agian to undo it
    We can test projects inside other projects aswell:
        ☐ Just like this
        ☐ Also we can fold the

Tags:
    ☐ We can add taks using the `@`, which we used earlier to estimate a time, but can also be used to create tags @this-is-a-tag
    ☐ Theres some special tags like @critical @low @high @today

Embedded todos:
    Embedded todos are TODOS that are spread across the codebase with uppercase TODO or FIXME
    We can create a new todo file for these with `Shift + Ctrl + P` and search for `Todo: Open Embedded`
    These will import the embedded todos and a link to that specific file aswell
    Embedded todos gets its own view in the `activity bar view`

Statistics:
    We can see how many todos are completed and how many are lefts and also a precentage at the lower bar
    For this file, it should say `1/12 (8%)`
    By hovering, it will provide more info, such as `11 Pending, 1 Done, 0 Cancelled`

Timekeeping:
    When we `start` a taks, a timer will show at the bottom bar
        By hovering it will show exactly what task its recording
        By clicking on it it will put the mouse focus on exactly that task
        If we happen to start another task, while a previous task is running, the previous task will pause and a new timer will start running
            When we finish that task, the previous timer will continue